; One variable: CameraAttributesPractical.auto_exposure_enabled over a procedural sky. Godot divides
; the exposure by the luminance of the frame, held between the bounds, so the sky and the ground draw
; lighter than with the exposure off. The luminance is the average over the frame's top left region,
; which holds the sky: a frame read from its bottom row averages the ground alone and draws far
; brighter, so no other scene shows that order.
